        "original_id": "b8b609ee-07ed-5db8-9093-f5af1405bf0e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: EdChoice, Cato Institute's Center for Educational Freedom\n- People: Milton Friedman, Rose Director Friedman, Jason Bedrick\n- Roles: Director of Policy, adjunct scholar, policy analyst\n- Topics: economics, educational policy\n\nFacts:\n- Milton Friedman was born on July 31, 1912, and died on November 16, 2006.\n- Milton Friedman was an American economist who received the 1976 Nobel Memorial Prize in Economic Sciences for research on consumption analysis, monetary history and theory, and the complexity of stabilization policy.\n- EdChoice was founded in 1996 by Milton Friedman and his wife, economist Rose Director Friedman.\n- Jason Bedrick is the Director of Policy at EdChoice.\n- Jason Bedrick is an adjunct scholar at the Cato Institute's Center for Educational Freedom.\n- Jason Bedrick previously worked as a policy analyst at the Cato Institute's Center for Educational Freedom.",
